  choiceText: 
  options:
  - id: afb49af8-9cc8-441c-8f29-a12d4ef26ef5
    text: "You speak to the design team who confirm that the level can be built up
      by putting insulation under the new flooring. They will need to update their
      design to show this and inform the client. You can attempt to recover these
      costs from the screeder via a contra-charge. It will cost \xA310 per m2."
    profit: -4
    profitStatus: 0
    satisfaction: -15
    satisfactionStatus: 0
    nextSequence: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98aa08deaac3ade4593be111e87c6f13, type: 2}
  - id: afb49af8-9cc8-441c-8f29-a12d4ef26ef5
    text: "You speak to the floorer who confirms that they can break out the existing
      screed and pour new screed themselves. It will be time consuming and cost \xA315
      per m2 but the design does not need to be updated and other works could carry
      on in other areas so there would be no overall programme delay and the client
      would not need to be notified."
    profit: -1
    profitStatus: 0
    satisfaction: 0
    satisfactionStatus: 1
    nextSequence: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 14ca4c5120aa2c4489aff0c30c32ffc7, type: 2}
  - id: afb49af8-9cc8-441c-8f29-a12d4ef26ef5
    text: Contractually you believe that the screeder is required to return and make
      good for free. You speak to the screeder and demand they return. They are extremely
      reluctant and demand a meeting with your team.
    profit: -3
    profitStatus: 0
    satisfaction: -20
    satisfactionStatus: 0
    nextSequence: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 090d8c9d33cb12c4089227a525d0d7ed, type: 2}
